# scenario-data-models

## Core Scenario Structure
Location: real-world-decisions/js/data.js

The scenario data models are organized into six primary categories aligned with therapeutic life skills development:

- Everyday Choices
- Social Situations  
- School & Work
- Family Relationships
- Money Management
- Health & Safety

Each scenario contains:
- Difficulty level indicators
- Social skill classification tags
- Targeted learning outcome definitions

## Learning Outcome Model
Scenarios are mapped to therapeutic assessment components:
- Problem Identification
- Options Analysis  
- Consequence Evaluation
- Impact Assessment
- Decision Making
- Action Planning

## Difficulty Classification
Implements progressive difficulty scaling with:
- Performance-based level adjustments
- Token-based scoring system:
  - Green: 5 points
  - Yellow: 3 points 
  - Red: 1 point

## Skill Categorization
Scenarios are tagged with relevant social competency markers used for:
- Therapeutic tracking
- Skill development progression
- Behavioral assessment alignment

## Game Mode Templates
Four specialized scenario delivery formats:
- Standard Challenge
- Tournament
- Skill Building  
- Quick Decision

Each mode contains unique scenario presentation and evaluation parameters aligned with specific therapeutic objectives.

